A||||3||Snowball||replacing outer window sweep||||8||
Z||000000||Snowball||06-06-2001||01:40 PM||||OK I got the inner door panel off removed the old inner window sweep lowered the window looked for some way to get the window out of the way but no luck. I can see the screws that hold on the outer sweep but the window is in the way. Local body shop said that I had to remove the door skin to get the window out of the track. ARE THEY FOR REAL? before I start a total rebuild I thought that I would ask here. If it makes any difference the car has power windows and mirrors. Help Please  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000001||mbramble||06-06-2001||01:48 PM||||Go to <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A>  click on TOOLS and you will see the Dew Wipe tool that you need to get those screws out.<P>I had a friend make me one by cutting off a phillips bit and welding it to a flat bar.  Wrapped the whole bar in electrical tape so as not to scratch the window.<p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 06-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Snowball||06-06-2001||02:36 PM||||Thanks Mike. the part is on the way. This forum is awsome. Can't wait to head south and meet some of you at one of the shows, maybe next year  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||Ronnie||06-06-2001||11:23 PM||||I made my own tool also. Once you get the tool to work with, loosen off on the window adjustment bolts , which will allow you to move the window glass in and out enough to access the screws a little better.<BR>Also , if you slot the screw holes in the new dew wipe, you can get the screws started , then slide the wipe onto the screws and tighten them. Just a little trick  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
